          "title": "You'll want to know: la broma",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la broma — \"the joke, the prank\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Era una broma, no te enfades. It was a joke, do not be angry."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Gastar una broma — to play a joke. En broma — jokingly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "broma comes from Greek brôma \"food\" (EtymDB), through Latin. It first named the shipworm that eats ship timber, then any nuisance, and at last a joke."
            }
          ]
        },
